soma patch of tiny_http 0.12.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0, licenses kept):
src/util/equal_reader.rs — Drop drains the unread body in 64 KiB chunks
instead of one allocation of the declared Content-Length.
src/client.rs, src/request.rs, src/util/refined_tcp_stream.rs — Request::respond_and_close
sends the response then shuts the socket down in both directions: a refused
framing (oversized / malformed body) closes the connection instead of
reading the bytes after it as a next request.
src/util/chunked.rs (used by src/request.rs) — a strict chunked decoder replaces
chunked_transfer::Decoder: trailers after the last chunk are read and discarded
(they were left on the socket as the next request), an EOF inside a chunk is an
error (a truncated body read as complete), chunk sizes are plain hex digits,
bare CR/LF are errors, and an error is sticky. soma serve answers any body read
error with 400 and closes the connection.
src/util/equal_reader.rs — an EOF before Content-Length bytes is an UnexpectedEof error.
